  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: The top-performing region is clearly scvi_n200 + multiprofile + transformer, with config_045 (vit_l + weighted) at 0.7250 as the current best, config_007 (vit_l + concat) at 0.7207, and config_035 (resnet50 + weighted) at 0.7131. The remaining untested configuration in this high-performing region is config_032 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + transformer + concat). This experiment tests whether the resnet50 + concat combination with transformer aggregation is competitive, completing the 2×2 factorial (image encoder × fusion) within the best aggregation setting. While I expect it to land around 0.71 (below config_045), it is the most informative remaining test in the proven high-accuracy region and rules out any unexpected synergy between resnet50 and concat fusion. No other untested configuration (avgpool variants, singleprofile, or non-scvi encoders) has a realistic chance of exceeding 0.7250. Expected relative cost: moderate-to-high (~5–6 GPU hours, comparable to config_035's 6.22), since it uses resnet50 with transformer aggregation. This is a justified expense given it is the last untested point in the top-performing subspace and only one experiment remains after this one."
}

